<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Sheikhdom of Abu Dhabi</h1><p class="st-meta">1761 CE – 1971 CE (approx.) · capital Abu Dhabi</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Al Nahyan sheikhdom of the Bani Yas, which grew from a pearling settlement into the oil-rich heart of the United Arab Emirates.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>According to tradition, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bani-yas">Bani Yas</a> tribesmen hunting on the island of Abu Dhabi found fresh water in 1761, and a settlement grew there. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-nahyan">Al Nahyan</a> sheikhs, leaders of the Bani Yas, moved their seat from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liwa-oasis">Liwa</a> oases to the island in the 1790s.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Abu Dhabi controlled a large desert hinterland, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liwa-oasis">Liwa</a> and part of the Buraimi oasis, and lived from pearling, dates and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camel">camels</a>. From 1820 it was one of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/trucial-states">Trucial States</a> under British protection. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zayed-bin-khalifa-al-nahyan">Zayed bin Khalifa</a>, ruling from 1855 to 1909, made it the strongest sheikhdom on the coast. The collapse of the pearl trade in the 1930s brought great poverty.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Oil was found offshore in 1958 and exported from 1962. In 1966 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zayed-bin-sultan-al-nahyan">Zayed bin Sultan Al Nahyan</a> replaced his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shakhbut-bin-sultan-al-nahyan">Shakhbut</a> and used the revenues for development. He led the creation of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-arab-emirates">United Arab Emirates</a> in 1971 and became its first president.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/sheikhdom-of-abu-dhabi.jpg" alt="Sheikhdom of Abu Dhabi" width="320" height="176"><figcaption>Image: Wadiia · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abu_dhabi_skylines_2014.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1761 CE – 1971 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Abu Dhabi</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Zayed bin Khalifa, Shakhbut bin Sultan, Zayed bin Sultan Al Nahyan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/united-arab-emirates">United Arab Emirates</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Abu Dhabi, Emirate of Abu Dhabi</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1866&amp;focus=sheikhdom-of-abu-dhabi" aria-label="Sheikhdom of Abu Dhabi on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6126 1277 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Sheikhdom of Abu Dhabi lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6446 1533L6439 1557M6446 1533L6446 1533M6446 1533L6466 1504"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6439 1557h0M6446 1533h0M6466 1504h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6446 1533h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6446 1533h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1866&amp;focus=sheikhdom-of-abu-dhabi">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
